===== STATUS: success =====
Question: What is PaperQA2?

PaperQA2 is a frontier language model agent optimized for improved factuality in scientific research tasks (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3). It functions as a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) system that decomposes scientific literature search and synthesis into multi-step agent tasks rather than treating them as direct procedures (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3, skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5).

The system incorporates multiple specialized components, including tools for paper search, evidence gathering with reranking and contextual summarization (RCS), answer generation, and citation traversal (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5). PaperQA2 parses papers using Grobid, ranks relevant chunks via dense vector retrieval and large language model reranking, and allows iterative search revision (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5).

PaperQA2 was designed using the LitQA2 benchmark and demonstrates superhuman performance on three realistic literature research tasks: information retrieval from scientific literature, summarization of scientific topics into cited Wikipedia-style articles, and contradiction detection within scientific papers (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3). On the LitQA2 benchmark, PaperQA2 achieved 85.2% precision and 66.0% accuracy, outperforming other RAG systems and achieving superhuman precision compared to PhD-level human annotators (73.8%) (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 3-5). The system can identify contradictions in biology papers at scale with 70% validation by human experts and reduces hallucinations through targeted prompting strategies (skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 1-3, skarlinski2024languageagentsachieve pages 17-19).

